1
00:00:01,568 --> 00:00:04,852
Mystery of the Police Car Robot!

2
00:00:47,731 --> 00:00:49,564
I almost had it...

3
00:00:50,310 --> 00:00:50,991
Hm?

4
00:00:51,692 --> 00:00:54,215
Ah! I'm gonna be late for school!

5
00:01:00,283 --> 00:01:01,651
Hm?

6
00:01:01,850 --> 00:01:03,454
Huh, what's that?

7
00:01:27,733 --> 00:01:30,406
A... robot?

8
00:01:30,462 --> 00:01:32,417
This ends now, Mega Trucker!

9
00:01:32,417 --> 00:01:34,200
You're coming with me.

10
00:01:38,783 --> 00:01:41,823
Do you really think I'm just gonna play along nicely?!

11
00:01:44,972 --> 00:01:47,331
Look alive, I'm not done yet!

12
00:01:48,698 --> 00:01:50,340
This stubborn truck...!

13
00:01:55,789 --> 00:01:57,188
My BMX!

14
00:02:11,163 --> 00:02:12,859
There's a human here!

15
00:02:16,103 --> 00:02:18,180
Tch. This isn't over!

16
00:02:21,389 --> 00:02:22,276
Stop right there!

17
00:02:27,175 --> 00:02:30,889
What have you done to my bike?!

18
00:02:30,889 --> 00:02:33,567
And where did my helmet go?

19
00:02:43,543 --> 00:02:47,115
Hey, we'll be in middle school next year and you're still saying things like,

20
00:02:47,115 --> 00:02:49,639
"I saw a robot! I saw an alien!"

21
00:02:49,639 --> 00:02:51,961
I think he's finally lost it!

22
00:02:51,961 --> 00:02:54,120
Vance, you sounded just like him!

23
00:02:54,120 --> 00:02:56,533
I swear I saw it with my own two eyes!

24
00:02:56,533 --> 00:02:58,468
A police car transformed into a robot!

25
00:02:58,468 --> 00:03:00,788
Oh really? Then where's your proof, huh?

26
00:03:00,788 --> 00:03:02,235
Ughh...

27
00:03:02,235 --> 00:03:03,800
Look at my crushed BMX!

28
00:03:03,800 --> 00:03:07,169
Huh... sorry, but it looks like you fell off and broke your bike.

29
00:03:07,169 --> 00:03:11,336
Ah! So he made up a whole story just to blame a robot for that? Vance, you're sharp!

30
00:03:11,436 --> 00:03:15,509
You should have made up a more believable story, Jun.

31
00:03:15,509 --> 00:03:16,900
I don't think he's lying.

32
00:03:16,900 --> 00:03:17,836
Huh?

33
00:03:18,336 --> 00:03:20,348
And what do you mean by that, class president?

34
00:03:20,348 --> 00:03:23,143
Are you trying to say that Vance is wrong?!

35
00:03:23,143 --> 00:03:26,651
I know Jun isn't one to tell petty lies like that.

36
00:03:26,651 --> 00:03:29,947
As expected of Anna! You're the only one who believes in me!

37
00:03:29,947 --> 00:03:32,807
I think he's probably just mistaken.

38
00:03:36,312 --> 00:03:39,180
Ugh... she didn't believe me either...

39
00:03:39,180 --> 00:03:41,319
I believe your robot story.

40
00:03:42,751 --> 00:03:44,699
Theo!

41
00:03:46,223 --> 00:03:47,352
Security cameras?

42
00:03:47,352 --> 00:03:50,848
If what you said is true, something must have been caught on video!

43
00:03:50,848 --> 00:03:52,288
Alright!

44
00:03:53,603 --> 00:03:54,461
Huh?

45
00:03:55,204 --> 00:03:57,860
Yeah, so when I got here this morning, I saw-

46
00:03:57,860 --> 00:03:59,437
Huh? Jun!

47
00:04:00,639 --> 00:04:02,443
Jun, you're safe and sound!

48
00:04:02,443 --> 00:04:06,068
Stop it! I can't breathe!

49
00:04:06,068 --> 00:04:09,804
I was worried sick! When I got here this morning, this place was a mess!

50
00:04:09,804 --> 00:04:12,936
And then I found your bike and thought you got crushed too!

51
00:04:14,936 --> 00:04:17,713
Hehe... Sorry for worrying you.

52
00:04:18,129 --> 00:04:19,538
It's okay. Thank you.

53
00:04:19,737 --> 00:04:22,108
We'll be heading back to the station now.

54
00:04:22,108 --> 00:04:23,454
Thanks for stopping by!

55
00:04:23,454 --> 00:04:24,406
Here you go.

56
00:04:28,079 --> 00:04:30,302
Tell me, what brings you guys here?

57
00:04:30,302 --> 00:04:32,112
Show us the security footage!

58
00:04:32,747 --> 00:04:34,125
Huh?

59
00:04:37,379 --> 00:04:38,105
Right there!

60
00:04:38,105 --> 00:04:40,156
Rewind a little bit, please!

61
00:04:45,100 --> 00:04:46,557
This doesn't show us anything...

62
00:04:46,557 --> 00:04:48,629
Yeah, didn't even get the license plate.

63
00:04:48,629 --> 00:04:51,271
It would be nice to know the license plate for the police car-

64
00:04:51,271 --> 00:04:55,119
And what would you do with that? Would you go to the police station and ask,

65
00:04:55,119 --> 00:04:56,937
"Is there a car here that transforms into a robot?"

66
00:04:56,937 --> 00:04:59,161
I knew it! You don't believe me either!

67
00:04:59,161 --> 00:05:01,192
Who would believe something like that?

68
00:05:01,192 --> 00:05:04,173
If only there was some other clue...

69
00:05:04,173 --> 00:05:06,112
Hang on! I have this!

70
00:05:08,119 --> 00:05:10,393
I picked it up after all of that happened.

71
00:05:10,393 --> 00:05:12,502
Did the robots leave it behind?

72
00:05:12,502 --> 00:05:13,951
I think so.

73
00:05:13,951 --> 00:05:17,449
This looks like something you can buy anywhere these days.

74
00:05:25,548 --> 00:05:27,331
Stop messing around...

75
00:05:27,331 --> 00:05:31,516
Agh, I'm not! I really can't lift it! It's like it's glued to the table!

76
00:05:32,615 --> 00:05:34,286
Let me try.

77
00:05:36,644 --> 00:05:38,167
I can't move it at all, not even an inch!

78
00:05:38,266 --> 00:05:41,233
Don't be ridiculous. See?

79
00:05:41,233 --> 00:05:43,281
Agh! What's going on here?!

80
00:05:43,281 --> 00:05:45,735
That's what I should be asking you...

81
00:05:47,252 --> 00:05:50,158
Let's go look for a place where a dump truck might be parked.

82
00:05:50,158 --> 00:05:52,290
You guys never give up, do you?

83
00:05:52,290 --> 00:05:55,627
Are you sure you're not just trying to impress Anna?

84
00:05:55,627 --> 00:05:57,519
That's not it!

85
00:05:57,519 --> 00:05:58,624
I'll be back soon!

86
00:05:58,624 --> 00:06:01,319
And throw away that strange watch, will you?

87
00:06:01,319 --> 00:06:02,711
Alright, alright.

88
00:06:18,545 --> 00:06:21,788
Ugh... guess it wouldn't be that easy to find, right?

89
00:06:21,788 --> 00:06:24,670
There's no guarantee it'll even be in this town anymore.

90
00:06:24,970 --> 00:06:26,485
Stop it!

91
00:06:26,485 --> 00:06:27,596
Anna?!

92
00:06:28,199 --> 00:06:30,211
You got a problem, class president?

93
00:06:30,211 --> 00:06:32,273
Don't act so high-and-mighty just because you're head of the student council!

94
00:06:32,273 --> 00:06:36,627
I'm not! You're being vandals by painting over our city without permission!

95
00:06:36,927 --> 00:06:38,903
That's what I call acting high-and-mighty!

96
00:06:38,903 --> 00:06:43,987
Why do you care so much about this city? You want to get sprayed too?!

97
00:06:43,987 --> 00:06:45,105
Don't!

98
00:06:45,271 --> 00:06:46,297
Back off!

99
00:06:46,829 --> 00:06:47,891
J-Jun?

100
00:06:47,891 --> 00:06:50,230
Heh! So you want to play the hero?

101
00:06:50,230 --> 00:06:51,358
How's the robot hunt going?

102
00:06:51,358 --> 00:06:52,901
I'll find it soon!

103
00:06:52,901 --> 00:06:55,177
You sound confident!

104
00:06:59,560 --> 00:07:01,024
I stepped in poop.

105
00:07:01,824 --> 00:07:03,778
Rapid fire poop kick!!

106
00:07:03,778 --> 00:07:05,086
Get away, get away!

107
00:07:07,187 --> 00:07:09,685
Vance! How dare you! Aah!

108
00:07:10,786 --> 00:07:12,055
You really fell for it!

109
00:07:12,555 --> 00:07:14,396
- See you later, Anna!
- Jun!

110
00:07:14,396 --> 00:07:15,500
Get back here!

111
00:07:15,935 --> 00:07:16,987
I said stop! Hey!!

112
00:07:16,987 --> 00:07:18,711
You're so dead when we catch you!

113
00:07:24,036 --> 00:07:25,637
-Ravi!
-On it!

114
00:07:32,319 --> 00:07:33,543
Ta-da!

115
00:07:33,543 --> 00:07:34,968
Waahh! Not good!

116
00:07:38,588 --> 00:07:40,233
Nice try!

117
00:07:40,233 --> 00:07:42,836
Nowhere to run now!

118
00:07:42,836 --> 00:07:45,754
Hang on! Let's not resort to violence, you guys!

119
00:07:45,754 --> 00:07:46,939
Shut up!

120
00:07:47,740 --> 00:07:49,331
Hey! Give that back!

121
00:07:49,831 --> 00:07:52,637
This is for trying to trick me!

122
00:07:53,538 --> 00:07:54,295
Hey!

123
00:07:54,295 --> 00:07:55,749
Quit struggling!

124
00:08:01,973 --> 00:08:03,567
I said, stop it!

125
00:08:14,468 --> 00:08:15,663
What's going on?

126
00:08:30,946 --> 00:08:32,600
What are you trying to pull now?!

127
00:08:33,764 --> 00:08:36,264
Change... Up!

128
00:08:41,971 --> 00:08:44,778
Is that... the robot from before...? (FX-italic)

129
00:08:55,259 --> 00:08:56,187
Wha...

130
00:08:56,187 --> 00:08:57,788
A robot! Jun was telling the truth!

131
00:08:57,788 --> 00:08:59,557
Come on, that's impossible!

132
00:08:59,557 --> 00:09:01,442
You must be seeing things!

133
00:09:01,442 --> 00:09:02,990
But you saw it too, Vance...

134
00:09:02,990 --> 00:09:06,019
Listen up! You better not tell anyone about this,

135
00:09:06,019 --> 00:09:09,711
unless you want to be called a liar too, got it?

136
00:09:09,711 --> 00:09:11,725
Alright...

137
00:09:15,456 --> 00:09:16,764
W-What's going on?!

138
00:09:24,006 --> 00:09:25,599
How is it driving by itself?!

139
00:09:25,599 --> 00:09:26,831
Nice to meet you.

140
00:09:26,831 --> 00:09:27,447
Huh?

141
00:09:27,447 --> 00:09:29,899
I am Blue Cop, from the planet Machina.

142
00:09:29,899 --> 00:09:30,889
Blue Cop?

143
00:09:32,971 --> 00:09:37,528
Agh! So does that mean I'm inside a robot's stomach right now?

144
00:09:39,672 --> 00:09:41,605
Help, I've been eaten by a robot!!

145
00:09:41,605 --> 00:09:43,946
Huh? What's the matter?

146
00:09:43,946 --> 00:09:45,869
Get me out before I'm digested!

147
00:09:45,869 --> 00:09:46,979
Digested?

148
00:09:46,979 --> 00:09:49,980
Wait, not out the backside. Spit me back up!

149
00:09:49,980 --> 00:09:53,418
I am a mechanical lifeform. I do not digest nor excrete.

150
00:09:53,418 --> 00:09:54,899
Oh, really?

151
00:09:54,899 --> 00:09:56,587
It's going to get a little bumpy.

152
00:09:56,879 --> 00:09:58,644
Aah!

153
00:10:01,798 --> 00:10:05,668
My home planet, Machina, was completely destroyed in a giant explosion.

154
00:10:05,668 --> 00:10:06,817
Destroyed?

155
00:10:06,817 --> 00:10:12,533
Ever since arriving on this planet, I have pretended to be a car so as not to alarm the natives.

156
00:10:12,533 --> 00:10:15,692
As your kind says, a tree is best hidden in a forest.

157
00:10:15,692 --> 00:10:17,115
I'm surprised you know that saying...

158
00:10:17,716 --> 00:10:19,875
I have to live on Earth now.

159
00:10:20,575 --> 00:10:24,836
So I am trying my best to learn as much about this planet as I can.

160
00:10:29,092 --> 00:10:31,368
I like this planet very much.

161
00:10:31,368 --> 00:10:34,629
However, there are some of my kind who have not adjusted to life here yet.

162
00:10:34,629 --> 00:10:36,999
You mean, like that dump truck from yesterday?

163
00:10:36,999 --> 00:10:38,778
He's not the only one.

164
00:10:38,778 --> 00:10:43,235
There are more Metal Cardbots hiding on Earth who I have yet to identify.

165
00:10:43,235 --> 00:10:47,863
I only wish to help them, so that they do not harm the natives of this planet. If I don't succeed,

166
00:10:47,863 --> 00:10:52,432
Wait, wait, wait! Why are you telling me all this?

167
00:10:52,432 --> 00:10:55,778
Because it looks like the Metal Breath chose you, sir.

168
00:10:55,778 --> 00:10:57,831
Metal Breath?

169
00:10:57,831 --> 00:11:01,581
The Metal Breath can only be possessed by the chosen one.

170
00:11:01,581 --> 00:11:05,509
It is said that the one who wields the Metal Breath will become the king that will shackle all of the Metal Cardbots.

171
00:11:05,509 --> 00:11:06,918
K-king?

172
00:11:06,918 --> 00:11:10,533
Uh! Pardon my mistake. I mean... the boss? The master?

173
00:11:10,533 --> 00:11:12,966
So, you mean... someone important?

174
00:11:12,966 --> 00:11:14,682
Yes sir! That's correct.

175
00:11:14,682 --> 00:11:18,163
No way! I haven't even been class president or anything!

176
00:11:18,163 --> 00:11:22,211
Please. I ask that you lend me your strength, sir.

177
00:11:22,211 --> 00:11:25,259
Hmm... alright!

178
00:11:25,259 --> 00:11:26,697
But on one condition!

179
00:11:26,697 --> 00:11:27,740
What's that?

180
00:11:27,740 --> 00:11:30,975
My name is Jun Grant! Call me Jun, not sir!

181
00:11:31,173 --> 00:11:32,259
Yes, Jun!

182
00:11:32,759 --> 00:11:33,655
And one more thing!

183
00:11:35,153 --> 00:11:39,365
My BMX that your friend crushed! You'll need to compensate me for that!

184
00:11:39,365 --> 00:11:40,764
What?!

